# Limits of Schemes, Chapter 1: Introduction

The source section describes the chapter's topics: limits of inverse systems
of schemes over directed sets with affine transition maps, absolute Noetherian
approximation, the characterization of schemes locally of finite presentation
over a base by limit-preservation of their associated functors of points, the
affineness of the image of an affine under an integral morphism, and variants
of Chow's lemma.  These are chapter-level motivation and pointers to later
sections, not precise
definitions, assertions, identities, diagrams, exact sequences, examples,
hypotheses, or mathematically meaningful warnings requiring Lean declarations.
The section also gives a bibliography reference to EGA.
